# Netlify rules, evaluated top to bottom — first match wins. Everything in
# ui/public/ is copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite, which is how this file
# reaches Netlify without appearing in the build output.

# --- Canonicalize onto the custom domain ------------------------------------
# Setting revops.frogslayer.com as the primary domain in the Netlify UI is not
# enough on its own: the SPA catch-all below matches every path and returns 200,
# and _redirects rules are evaluated before Netlify's automatic
# subdomain -> primary redirect, so that redirect never fires. Hence the explicit
# rules, and hence their position ABOVE the catch-all.
#
# `!` forces the redirect even where a real file exists — without it, static
# assets under /assets/* would be served from the netlify.app origin instead.
http://fs-revenue-ops.netlify.app/*   https://revops.frogslayer.com/:splat  301!
https://fs-revenue-ops.netlify.app/*  https://revops.frogslayer.com/:splat  301!

# --- SPA fallback ------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-side routing means /invoices, /approvals etc. exist only in the browser;
# Netlify would otherwise look for a file at that path and 404. Status 200 (not
# 301/302) so the address bar is preserved and the router sees the real path.
/*  /index.html  200
